        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(channels): reuse loaded plugin lookup view",
        "body": "Closes #105972\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where message processing repeatedly sorted the loaded channel registry and rebuilt two lookup maps whenever callers read channel plugins from an unchanged runtime registry.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe loaded registry view now uses one lifecycle-owned, single-slot cache keyed by the active runtime channel snapshot. Registry version changes still rebuild the deterministic sorted list and maps; unchanged snapshots reuse them. The separate linear-scan reader is folded into the canonical loaded-registry module so all loaded-only reads use one lookup path.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRepeated outbound, reply, and agent-message channel lookups avoid redundant registry iteration, sorting, and map allocation. Channel ordering and lookup behavior are unchanged; there are no config or plugin API changes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before: the regression test on `cb5fc0ea8a53bafdd92e5fa106574fb559d7e7fe` observed three derived-view builds across three reads (`expected 3 to be 1`).\n- After: the same test observes one build for the unchanged version and exactly one additional build after the registry version changes; deterministic `alpha`, `zeta` ordering is retained.\n- Rebased Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxctdqkj3m772k62dh5zh2nj`: 46 focused channel/outbound tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox: `pnpm build`, all core/extension production and test `tsgo` lanes, full core/extension lint, and `pnpm format:check` passed.\n- Exact dependency-gate reproduction confirms the snapshot type is no longer a stale deadcode-baseline entry. Remaining current-main gate failures are unrelated sidebar export and QA-lab mock drift; the touched lint, type, build, format, and focused test surfaces pass.\n\nAI-assisted: yes (Codex).\n",
